  "description": "The proposal is a Full Planning Application for the amalgamation of the existing ground-floor and first-floor flats into a single residential unit (Class C3). The primary objective is to consolidate these two smaller, self-contained units to create one larger, high-quality family home.\n\nDetails of the Works\nInternal Alterations: The project involves internal reconfigurations to facilitate a connection between the ground and first floor level.\nExternal Appearance: There are no proposed changes to the external appearance of the building or the street scene; all works are strictly internal.\nUse Class: The residential use of the site remains unchanged under Class C3 (dwellinghouses).\n",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>"
